From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:47:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: leave capture buffers for display with
 dynamic DPB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With dynamic DPB the firmware may keep its whole minimum DPB as
references at once. A client that allocates only that minimum plus one
or two buffers then has almost none left to display while the next
frame decodes. Chromium allocates the driver's minimum plus 2: for a
3840x2160 VP9 clip on the Pixel 7 (minimum 10) it decoded at about
24 fps and dropped 131 of 468 frames at 30 fps.

Give such clients at least four buffers more than the minimum. With it
Chromium drops 4 of 582 frames of the same clip (looping, the drops are
at the loop points), and H.264 3840x2160 still drops none. GStreamer's
output stays bit-exact against vp9dec and avdec_h264 at 3840x2160.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index beb6bc32e..b7615ba8d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -1022,6 +1022,12 @@ static int s5p_mfc_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *vq,
 		/* Setup buffer count */
 		if (*buf_count < ctx->pb_count)
 			*buf_count = ctx->pb_count;
+		/*
+		 * With dynamic DPB the firmware can hold all of its minimum
+		 * at once; leave some for the client to display.
+		 */
+		if (dev->dynamic_dpb && *buf_count < ctx->pb_count + 4)
+			*buf_count = ctx->pb_count + 4;
 		if (!dev->dynamic_dpb &&
 		    *buf_count > ctx->pb_count + MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB)
 			*buf_count = ctx->pb_count + MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB;
